# 基础词 Unit15
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 基础词Unit15核心词汇

{{qualify}}{{/ˈkwɒlɪfaɪ}}{{v. 使合格；具有资格}}{{Her experience qualifies her for the position.}}
{{quality}}{{/ˈkwɒləti}}{{n. 质量；品质}}{{The quality of the product is excellent.}}
{{quantity}}{{/ˈkwɒntəti}}{{n. 数量；大量}}{{A large quantity of food was wasted.}}
{{quarter}}{{/ˈkwɔːtər}}{{n. 四分之一；季度}}{{The company reported strong results for the first quarter.}}
{{quest}}{{/kwest}}{{n. 探索；追求}}{{The quest for knowledge drives scientific research.}}
{{quote}}{{/kwəʊt}}{{v./n. 引用；报价}}{{She quoted a famous line from Shakespeare.}}
{{race}}{{/reɪs}}{{n./v. 比赛；种族；赛跑}}{{The horse race attracted thousands of spectators.}}
{{radical}}{{/ˈrædɪkl}}{{adj./n. 激进的；根本的}}{{The government introduced radical reforms.}}
{{rage}}{{/reɪdʒ}}{{n./v. 愤怒；肆虐}}{{The storm raged for three days.}}
{{raise}}{{/reɪz}}{{v. 举起；提高；筹集}}{{They raised funds for the charity.}}
{{random}}{{/ˈrændəm}}{{adj. 随机的；任意的}}{{The numbers were selected at random.}}
{{range}}{{/reɪndʒ}}{{n./v. 范围；山脉；排列}}{{The store offers a wide range of products.}}
{{rank}}{{/ræŋk}}{{n./v. 等级；排名}}{{The university ranks among the top 10 in the world.}}
{{rapid}}{{/ˈræpɪd}}{{adj. 迅速的；快的}}{{The city has experienced rapid growth.}}
{{rare}}{{/reər}}{{adj. 稀有的；罕见的}}{{This is a rare species of bird.}}
{{rate}}{{/reɪt}}{{n./v. 比率；评价；速率}}{{The unemployment rate has dropped this year.}}
{{rational}}{{/ˈræʃnəl}}{{adj. 理性的；合理的}}{{We need to make rational decisions.}}
{{raw}}{{/rɔː}}{{adj. 生的；未加工的；原始的}}{{The factory imports raw materials from abroad.}}
{{react}}{{/riˈækt}}{{v. 反应；起化学反应}}{{How did she react to the news?}}
{{realistic}}{{/ˌriːəˈlɪstɪk}}{{adj. 现实的；逼真的}}{{We should set realistic goals.}}
{{realm}}{{/relm}}{{n. 领域；王国}}{{She made important contributions to the realm of science.}}
{{reasonable}}{{/ˈriːznəbl}}{{adj. 合理的；公道的}}{{The price is very reasonable for the quality.}}
{{rebel}}{{/ˈrebl}}{{n./v. 叛乱者；反抗}}{{The rebels fought against the government.}}
{{recall}}{{/rɪˈkɔːl}}{{v./n. 回忆；召回}}{{I can't recall where I put my keys.}}
{{receipt}}{{/rɪˈsiːt}}{{n. 收据；收到}}{{Please keep the receipt for your records.}}
{{recover}}{{/rɪˈkʌvər}}{{v. 恢复；收回}}{{She has fully recovered from her illness.}}
{{recruit}}{{/rɪˈkruːt}}{{v./n. 招聘；新成员}}{{The company is recruiting new graduates.}}
{{reduce}}{{/rɪˈdjuːs}}{{v. 减少；降低}}{{The company reduced its workforce by 10%.}}
{{refer}}{{/rɪˈfɜːr}}{{v. 提到；参考；转介}}{{Please refer to the handbook for details.}}
{{reflect}}{{/rɪˈflekt}}{{v. 反映；反射；思考}}{{The lake reflected the mountains beautifully.}}
{{reform}}{{/rɪˈfɔːm}}{{n./v. 改革；改良}}{{The education reform aims to improve teaching quality.}}
{{refuse}}{{/rɪˈfjuːz}}{{v. 拒绝；回绝}}{{She refused to accept the unfair offer.}}
{{regard}}{{/rɪˈɡɑːd}}{{v./n. 看待；尊重；方面}}{{He is highly regarded in his field.}}
{{region}}{{/ˈriːdʒən}}{{n. 地区；区域}}{{The tropical region has a warm climate all year.}}
{{register}}{{/ˈredʒɪstər}}{{v./n. 登记；注册}}{{She registered for the online course.}}
{{regulate}}{{/ˈreɡjuleɪt}}{{v. 管理；调节；规范}}{{The government regulates the financial industry.}}
{{reject}}{{/rɪˈdʒekt}}{{v. 拒绝；驳回}}{{The committee rejected the proposal.}}
{{relate}}{{/rɪˈleɪt}}{{v. 与…有关；叙述}}{{The article relates to the current economic situation.}}
{{release}}{{/rɪˈliːs}}{{v./n. 释放；发行；发布}}{{The movie will be released next month.}}
{{relevant}}{{/ˈreləvənt}}{{adj. 相关的；切题的}}{{Please provide relevant documents for the application.}}
{{reliable}}{{/rɪˈlaɪəbl}}{{adj. 可靠的；可信赖的}}{{She is a reliable colleague.}}
{{relief}}{{/rɪˈliːf}}{{n. 缓解；救济；浮雕}}{{The medicine provided quick relief from the pain.}}
{{reluctant}}{{/rɪˈlʌktənt}}{{adj. 不情愿的；勉强的}}{{He was reluctant to admit his mistake.}}
{{rely}}{{/rɪˈlaɪ}}{{v. 依赖；依靠}}{{You can rely on me for support.}}
{{remain}}{{/rɪˈmeɪn}}{{v. 保持；剩余；留下}}{{The door remained open throughout the night.}}
{{remark}}{{/rɪˈmɑːk}}{{n./v. 评论；谈论}}{{She made a remark about the weather.}}
{{remedy}}{{/ˈremədi}}{{n./v. 补救办法；治疗}}{{There is no easy remedy for this problem.}}
{{remote}}{{/rɪˈməʊt}}{{adj. 遥远的；偏僻的}}{{The village is in a remote area of the country.}}
{{remove}}{{/rɪˈmuːv}}{{v. 移除；去除}}{{Please remove your shoes before entering.}}
{{render}}{{/ˈrendər}}{{v. 使成为；提供；呈递}}{{The accident rendered him unconscious.}}
{{renew}}{{/rɪˈnjuː}}{{v. 更新；续期；恢复}}{{She renewed her passport before the trip.}}
{{rent}}{{/rent}}{{n./v. 租金；租用}}{{The rent for the apartment is 3000 yuan per month.}}
{{repair}}{{/rɪˈpeər}}{{v./n. 修理；修复}}{{The car needs to be repaired.}}
{{repeat}}{{/rɪˈpiːt}}{{v./n. 重复；重做}}{{Please repeat the question more slowly.}}
{{replace}}{{/rɪˈpleɪs}}{{v. 替换；取代}}{{Robots may replace humans in some jobs.}}
{{represent}}{{/ˌreprɪˈzent}}{{v. 代表；象征}}{{The dove represents peace.}}
{{reputation}}{{/ˌrepjuˈteɪʃn}}{{n. 名誉；声望}}{{The company has a good reputation for quality.}}
{{request}}{{/rɪˈkwest}}{{n./v. 请求；要求}}{{She made a request for more time.}}
{{require}}{{/rɪˈkwaɪər}}{{v. 需要；要求}}{{The job requires strong communication skills.}}
{{rescue}}{{/ˈreskjuː}}{{v./n. 营救；解救}}{{The firefighters rescued the trapped passengers.}}
{{research}}{{/rɪˈsɜːtʃ}}{{n./v. 研究；调查}}{{The research was conducted over three years.}}
{{resemble}}{{/rɪˈzembl}}{{v. 像；类似于}}{{She resembles her mother in many ways.}}
{{reserve}}{{/rɪˈzɜːv}}{{v./n. 保留；预订；储备}}{{I'd like to reserve a table for two.}}
{{resign}}{{/rɪˈzaɪn}}{{v. 辞职；放弃}}{{He resigned from his position as CEO.}}
{{resist}}{{/rɪˈzɪst}}{{v. 抵抗；抵制}}{{The material resists heat and water.}}
{{resolve}}{{/rɪˈzɒlv}}{{v./n. 解决；决心}}{{They resolved the conflict through negotiation.}}
{{resort}}{{/rɪˈzɔːt}}{{n./v. 度假胜地；求助于}}{{The beach resort is popular with tourists.}}
{{resource}}{{/rɪˈsɔːs}}{{n. 资源；办法}}{{We must use our natural resources wisely.}}
{{respond}}{{/rɪˈspɒnd}}{{v. 回答；反应}}{{She responded quickly to the emergency.}}
{{responsible}}{{/rɪˈspɒnsəbl}}{{adj. 负责的；有责任心的}}{{Who is responsible for this mess?}}
{{restore}}{{/rɪˈstɔːr}}{{v. 恢复；修复}}{{The old painting was carefully restored.}}
{{restrict}}{{/rɪˈstrɪkt}}{{v. 限制；约束}}{{Access to the area is restricted.}}
{{retain}}{{/rɪˈteɪn}}{{v. 保持；保留}}{{The company retained all its employees.}}
{{retire}}{{/rɪˈtaɪər}}{{v. 退休；撤退}}{{He retired at the age of 60.}}
{{reveal}}{{/rɪˈviːl}}{{v. 揭示；透露}}{{The investigation revealed surprising facts.}}
{{revenue}}{{/ˈrevənjuː}}{{n. 收入；税收}}{{The company's revenue increased by 20%.}}
{{reverse}}{{/rɪˈvɜːs}}{{v./adj./n. 颠倒；相反的；背面}}{{The court reversed the decision.}}
{{review}}{{/rɪˈvjuː}}{{v./n. 审查；评论；复习}}{{The professor reviewed the students' papers.}}
{{revise}}{{/rɪˈvaɪz}}{{v. 修订；修改}}{{She revised her essay before submitting it.}}
{{revolution}}{{/ˌrevəˈluːʃn}}{{n. 革命；旋转}}{{The industrial revolution transformed society.}}
{{reward}}{{/rɪˈwɔːd}}{{n./v. 奖赏；报酬}}{{Hard work will eventually bring its reward.}}
{{rhythm}}{{/ˈrɪðəm}}{{n. 节奏；韵律}}{{The music had a lively rhythm.}}
{{rid}}{{/rɪd}}{{v. 使摆脱；除去}}{{She rid herself of bad habits.}}
{{rigid}}{{/ˈrɪdʒɪd}}{{adj. 严格的；僵硬的}}{{The rules are too rigid to allow exceptions.}}
{{risk}}{{/rɪsk}}{{n./v. 风险；冒…的风险}}{{There is a risk of flooding in the area.}}
{{rival}}{{/ˈraɪvl}}{{n./adj./v. 竞争对手；竞争的}}{{The two companies have been rivals for years.}}
{{rob}}{{/rɒb}}{{v. 抢劫；剥夺}}{{The bank was robbed last night.}}
{{role}}{{/rəʊl}}{{n. 角色；作用}}{{Education plays a key role in personal development.}}
{{root}}{{/ruːt}}{{n. 根；根源}}{{The root of the problem is lack of communication.}}
{{rough}}{{/rʌf}}{{adj. 粗糙的；大致的；艰难的}}{{The road was rough and hard to drive on.}}
{{rouse}}{{/raʊz}}{{v. 唤醒；激起}}{{The speech roused the crowd to action.}}
{{routine}}{{/ruːˈtiːn}}{{n./adj. 常规；日常的}}{{Exercise is part of her daily routine.}}
{{royal}}{{/ˈrɔɪəl}}{{adj. 王室的；皇家的}}{{The royal family attended the ceremony.}}
{{ruin}}{{/ˈruːɪn}}{{v./n. 毁灭；废墟}}{{The earthquake ruined many historic buildings.}}
{{rural}}{{/ˈrʊərəl}}{{adj. 农村的；乡下的}}{{Rural areas often lack access to healthcare.}}
{{rush}}{{/rʌʃ}}{{v./n. 冲；急忙；高峰期}}{{Everyone rushed to the exit when the alarm sounded.}}
